  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Domain requires this callback even for a storage-only consumer. The\n delegation test must use only node_path; discovering edges would be\n an unwanted graph access, which this guard rejects. Traversal fixtures\n separately exercise edge discovery."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` is in the permitted form and is right.\n\n- **Form:** It is a fenced citation with commentary on an explicitly declared function that has a body. That is the form a function-level coverage exception takes.\n- **Substantive reason:** The function body is only `panic!(\"storage operations must not discover graph edges\")`. It exists because `Domain` requires the callback. `StoredGraph` is a storage-only fixture, so the guard is meant never to run, and a passing test never executes it. That is a real reason for the zero coverage, not just difficulty.\n- **Agrees with the source:** I checked each claim against the current code.\n  - The delegation test, `tests/storage.rs#fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]`, calls only `load_evidence`, `store_evidence` and `node_path`. It never discovers edges, so it matches the claim that the test uses only `node_path`.\n  - In `stored_graph.rs`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` delegate to `FileEvidenceStorage` through `node_path` alone. Neither calls `outgoing_edges`.\n  - The panic message matches the \"unwanted graph access\" the commentary describes.\n  - Other fixtures implement `outgoing_edges` for real: `tests/contracts.rs#impl[Application/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` and the `Relationships` `Domain` impl in `tests/contracts.rs`. That is consistent with \"traversal fixtures separately exercise edge discovery\". I did not trace those fixtures' tests to confirm they execute the callback.",
